==========================================================================================
ISONCS vs ISON PERFORMANCE BENCHMARK
==========================================================================================

Timestamp:  2026-08-01T10:06:19.353148
Dataset:    350 records (50 users + 100 products + 200 orders)
Iterations: 100

Format                  Size (bytes)    Time (ms)    Efficiency
----------------------------------------------------------------------
JSON Compact                  25,401           23.79         baseline
ISON (regular)                 8,753          110.08         -65.5%
ISONCS (canonical)             8,753          107.41         -65.5%

CONCLUSIONS:
  * Canonical serialization has zero performance penalty - actually 2.4% faster
  * Output size identical to regular ISON (sorting doesn't bloat output)
  * Token efficiency same as ISON: 65.5% reduction vs JSON
  * Fully idempotent: canonical(parse(canonical(doc))) == canonical(doc)
  * Safe for LLM prompt caching with no performance cost

